diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..778aadf 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,8 +2,27 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+## Event delivery
+
+An active webhook receives an asynchronous HTTP `POST` when one of its subscribed actions occurs on its board. Delivery is queued only after the event commits. Inactive webhooks and unsubscribed actions do not receive events. Queued deliveries are skipped if the webhook has since been deactivated or the card has moved to another board.
+
+The request uses `Content-Type: application/json`. Its body contains the event's `id`, `action`, `created_at`, action-specific `particulars`, `board`, `creator`, and `eventable` (a card or comment in the API's normal representation). URLs include the event's account slug. Recognized Slack, Campfire, and Basecamp chat webhook URLs instead receive their respective `text`, `body`, and `content` message payloads.
+
+Requests include these headers:
+
+- `X-Webhook-Id`: the delivery's stable identifier, also shown in the delivery log.
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: the event's creation time in UTC, in ISO 8601 format.
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: the hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the **raw request body**, keyed with the webhook's `signing_secret`. Compare signatures using a constant-time comparison before processing a request.
+
+Each event/webhook pair gets one delivery attempt. Duplicate jobs do not repeat the POST, including after delivery logs expire. HTTP errors, redirects, and timeouts are not retried; redirects are not followed. Receivers must resolve to public IP addresses.
+
+Exactly-once processing cannot be guaranteed across HTTP: after a timeout or a worker interruption, the receiver may have processed a request even though Fizzy could not record its response. Fizzy does not resend such requests. Receivers can use `X-Webhook-Id` to deduplicate their own processing.
+
+A `2xx` response is successful. Other HTTP responses and connection errors count as failures. A webhook is automatically deactivated when its failure streak reaches **at least ten consecutive failures and spans at least one hour**. A success or manual reactivation resets the streak. Delivery logs are retained for seven days, with expired entries removed by the cleanup task every 15 minutes.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
+
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
 
 __Response:__
